  "chemical_intuition": [
    {
      "id": "authors-transport-explanation",
      "title": "Authors’ transport interpretation",
      "summary": "Authors attribute performance gains to larger CdS/PbS interfacial area, direct transport through ordered CdS rods and shorter carrier diffusion paths. Too few PbS layers leave incomplete coverage; excess overlay may increase recombination. Band energies in Figure 3c are taken from references 24 and 28, not measured here. Proposed follow-up: tune rod crystallinity, spacing/length and contacts.",
